<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dungan Revolt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dungan revolts, Dungan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dungan Revolt was a major uprising of Muslim Hui and other peoples in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in the 1860s and 1870s. It devastated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> and led to the temporary loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> before Qing forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zuo-zongtang">Zuo Zongtang</a> reconquered the region. It was one of several mid-nineteenth-century rebellions that strained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>.</p></div>
